(LST2-81 — the `otherwise` catch-all: it supplies a final alternative that
 runs when no `but if` matched, replacing the base action. The spelling
 the manual gives (bare `otherwise`) works after an `append` base but is a
 parse error after a `print` base; `but otherwise` works after both. See
 Discrepancy 2. This probe uses the spelling that works everywhere.
 Also covers: LST2-85 (`otherwise` as a catch-all alternative).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-81.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   plain
   plain
   third
   plain
   plain
   third
   [8, 0, 8, 0]
)
print each step from 1 to 6,
    but if the step modulo 3 is equal to 0 print "third",
    but otherwise print "plain".

a list called kept is [].
append each step from 1 to 4 to kept,
    but if the step modulo 2 is equal to 0 append 0,
    otherwise append 8.
print kept.
